  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When a large trigger zone (such as an enter/exit trigger used for local culling) completely envelops a smaller one, VR users will typically have trouble highlighting the smaller trigger with their hands and be unable to interact with interactive objects like buttons as a result. Desktop users generally won't experience this problem.\n\nThe current workarounds involve making trigger walls or double-layered hollow trigger boxes, but these solutions are inelegant. A fix would be much appreciated.",
